\tag{fnip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Where a component of the velocity vanishes}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{On the solution drawn in \ref{fnip-0011}, the voltage starts at
#{0}, rises, and then falls. The first component
of the velocity is positive while the voltage rises and negative while
it falls.}

\p{The two signs meet where that component is zero. The equations
assign a velocity at every point, so each component has a zero set in
the plane. What are those zero sets, and which curves do the solutions
follow among them?}
